winex11: Make a window transient for its first visible owner.

A window owned by a window that is never shown got WM_TRANSIENT_FOR on that owner's unmapped X window, and the window
manager gives a window transient for an unmapped one no stacking relation. Illustrator's floating panels (layered
OWL.Dock windows) are owned by an invisible "Palette Layer" window: KWin stacked the document window above them while
Wine kept them above it in X, so under XWayland the panels were drawn hidden behind the document yet took the clicks
over it (Transform, Color: invisible, and parts of the canvas ignored the mouse; 2026-10-23). Walk up the owner chain
to the first visible window, as Windows keeps owned windows above their owners.

--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -1123,6 +1123,16 @@
     if (owner)
     {
         owner = NtUserGetAncestor( owner, GA_ROOT );
+        /* An owner that is never shown has no mapped X window, and the window manager gives a window that is
+         * transient for an unmapped one no stacking relation: it stacked the owner's owner above it while Wine kept
+         * it above in X, so it was hidden yet took the clicks (Illustrator's floating panels are owned by an
+         * invisible "Palette Layer" window). Use the first visible window up the owner chain. */
+        while (!(NtUserGetWindowLongW( owner, GWL_STYLE ) & WS_VISIBLE))
+        {
+            HWND next = NtUserGetWindowRelative( owner, GW_OWNER );
+            if (!next) break;
+            owner = NtUserGetAncestor( next, GA_ROOT );
+        }
         owner_win = X11DRV_get_whole_window( owner );
     }
 
